# Screenshots Directory

This directory contains screenshots used in the documentation.

## Required Screenshots

The following screenshots are referenced in the documentation and should be added:

### Overview Document
1. `portal-overview.png` - Main portal interface
2. `dashboard-overview.png` - Full dashboard view
3. `logs-view.png` - Logs page with filtering options
4. `attack-map.png` - Attack origins world map
5. `attack-chart.png` - Attack timeline chart
6. `user-management.png` - User management interface
7. `waf-settings.png` - WAF enable/disable controls
8. `ip-ban-list.png` - IP ban management interface
9. `geo-access.png` - Geo-location access control settings
10. `notifications.png` - Notification configuration interface

### Dashboard Guide
11. `host-selector.png` - Host selector dropdown
12. `overview-stats.png` - Overview statistics cards
13. `time-filter.png` - Time range filter buttons
14. `recent-activity.png` - Recent Activity list

### Logs Guide
15. `logs-overview.png` - Full logs page view
16. `logs-header.png` - Logs page header with host selector
17. `logs-stats.png` - Statistics cards (Blocked Today, Allowed Today, Top Rule)
18. `logs-filters.png` - Search bar and filter dropdowns
19. `logs-table.png` - Logs table with columns and sample entries
20. `logs-pagination.png` - Pagination controls
21. `log-detail-panel.png` - Detailed log information panel

### Users Guide
22. `users-overview.png` - Users page showing team members table
23. `admin-limit.png` - Admin limit indicator
24. `add-user-modal.png` - Add user form

### Settings Guide
25. `settings-overview.png` - Settings page with tab navigation
26. `waf-settings.png` - WAF protection toggles for each domain
27. `summary-reports.png` - Summary reports configuration
28. `ip-ban-list.png` - List of banned IP addresses
29. `add-ip-ban.png` - Add IP ban modal
30. `geo-access-modes.png` - Geo access mode selection
31. `geo-access-config.png` - Country selection interface
32. `telegram-connect.png` - Telegram connection process
33. `notification-config.png` - Notification settings form

## Screenshot Guidelines

- Use PNG format for screenshots
- Maintain consistent resolution (recommended: 1920x1080 or higher)
- Crop to show relevant UI elements
- Use descriptive filenames
- Update this list when adding new screenshots
